The macOS CI guard skipped the very tests needed to verify transport
runtime behavior. Removed the guard for the two core lifecycle tests.
They use /tmp/ohya-e2e-* to avoid long macOS test paths at the control
plane's Unix socket. The existing macOS check job now executes them.
The workflow also gains a manual trigger.

Both core transport tests pass on Linux in 63.79 seconds. This does not
claim native macOS success. The host is Linux, and the updated workflow
cannot run remotely until the changes are published. No push is made.

Also adopted the existing migration 006 documentation update and closed
the obsolete malformed-line decision in NOTES.md. Related documentation
hunks were staged separately to preserve other uncommitted work.

Final verification: make check passes on the integrated working tree, including formatting, all Go tests, vet, and the comment checker. The memory-gate package also passes race detection.
